1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,050
我饿死了
I'm starving.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:04,360
那有可能是给我做的吗
Any chance that's for me?

3
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:05,610
不 是给老妈做的
Oh, no. It is for Mom.

4
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:07,380
我打算今晚做些坏决定
I'm planning on making some bad choices tonight,

5
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:08,920
我需要她站在我这一边
and I'm gonna need her on my side.

6
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:09,990
这种小算盘我从没实现过
I never realized the forethought

7
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:11,940
全都落空成了遗憾
that went into being a disappointment.

8
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,360
早啊 米奇舅舅 你来干什么
Hey, Uncle Mitch. What are you doing here?

9
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:18,360
什么干什么 今天可是米奇舅舅的生日欢乐日
What do you mean? It's Uncle Mitchell's Birthday Fun Day.

10
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:21,560
我们知道
We know!

11
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:22,830
当然啦
Yeah! Yeah!

12
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:25,300
你终于来兑现它了 我们好开心
We are so excited you are finally cashing this in.

13
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,140
我也是
Me too.

14
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,900
米奇舅舅上个生日的时候我们忘了送礼物
We forgot to get Uncle Mitchell a present for his last birthday.

15
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,950
所以我们想到了这个绝妙的主意
So, we came up with this great idea --

16
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:33,060
和我们共享欢乐一日的兑换券
A coupon for a fun day with the three of us.

17
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,970
这主意很完美 因为它不仅棒
It was perfect because it was so sweet

18
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:36,950
我们也不用真的去兑现
and we'd never have to do it.

19
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,200
我希望你准备好迎接第一个大惊喜了
I hope you're ready for your first big surprise!

20
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,510
准备好了
I am.

21
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,400
超级乐享煎蛋卷
It's a super-fun omelet!

22
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:43,780
是啊
Aww! Uh, yeah!

23
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:47,560
如果你在纳闷这究竟有什么超级乐享的
And if you were wondering what is so super-fun about that,

24
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:50,270
这是因为随蛋附送的是
is that it comes with a -- a side of, uh...

25
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,190
卢克的煎蛋卷舞
Luke's omelet dance!

26
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:56,840
别害羞 你不是都练了一周吗
Don't be shy. You've been practicing all week. Come on.

27
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,290
好吧
Okay. Uh...

28
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,600
*今天是你的生日*
*It's your birthday*

29
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,230
*我是个煎蛋卷*
*I'm an omelet*

30
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:05,370
*今天是你的生日*
*It's your birthday*

31
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,160
*我是个煎蛋卷*
*I'm an omelet*

32
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,850
今天是你的生日
It's your birthday

33
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:10,130
这真是个现实的梦魇
This is a living nightmare.

34
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:11,170
他为何会直接过来
Why would he just show up?

35
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:12,590
他不应该给我们先打个招呼吗
Shouldn't he have given us some notice?

36
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:14,180
我似乎记得他打电话说过这事
I kind of remember him calling about it,

37
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,370
但我肯定会记在手机上
But I would've put it in my phone --

38
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:16,790
-记着呢 -果不其然
- Oh, there it is. - Of course.

39
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,630
天啊 我现在是应该在照看一只猫的
Oh, my god. I'm supposed to be cat-sitting.

40
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:19,780
我们得想出个好主意
We have to figure out something good.

41
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,520
他总是在我们生日第一个打电话祝贺
He's the first to call us on our birthdays,

42
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,160
他还总会送给我们超赞的礼物
and he always gets us amazing presents.

43
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:25,820
你有在听我讲话吗
Are you even listening to me?

44
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,840
一只猫不吃东西能活多久
How long can a cat go without eating?

45
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,450
海莉 他是世界上最棒的舅舅
Haley, he is the best uncle there is.

46
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:33,030
这玩意儿可不能是我们的礼物
This cannot be our present.

47
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:34,630
*今天是你的生日*
*It's your birthday*

48
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:37,200
*我是个煎蛋卷 今天是你的生日*
*I'm an omelet, it's your birthday*

49
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,230
我不清楚这是什么情况 但我喜欢
I don't know what's happening, but I love it.

50
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:40,450
-今天是你的生日 -今天是我的生日
- It's your birthday. - It's my birthday.

51
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,040
-我是个煎蛋卷 -你是个煎蛋卷
- I'm an omelet. - You're an omelet.

52
00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:00,200
如果你再笑 我就自己弄我的指甲
If you're going to keep giggling, I'll do my own nails.

53
00:02:00,210 --> 00:02:02,920
抱歉 只不过太好笑了 这种情景置换
I'm sorry -- it's just funny, the juxtaposition.

54
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,330
我懂 因为我是亚裔
I get it -- I'm Asian.

55
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,870
这可是种族歧视 大爸
It's racist, Daddy.

56
00:02:08,090 --> 00:02:08,790
抱歉
Sorry.

57
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:12,120
莉莉 瞧瞧谁来了 我们可爱的加拿大房客
Lily, look who it is -- our lovely Canadian guests.

58
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,470
请进
Please come in.

59
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:14,570
楼上住的怎么样
How is everything upstairs?

60
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:15,830
楼上跟个宫殿一样
It's like a palace up there.

61
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:18,460
我还想着会不会遇到高登·平森特呢
I keep expecting to run into Gordon Pinsent.

62
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:21,330
抱歉
I'm sorry.

63
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:23,210
在楼下这里他不算是个大影星吗
Is he not a big movie star down here?

64
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:25,760
不算 但是感谢你们提供的瑞安·雷诺兹
No. But thank you for Ryan Reynolds.

65
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:28,880
还有件事 我们要去中国剧院
One little thing -- we're going to see the handprints

66
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:30,680
看星光大道的手印 我担心
at the Chinese Theater, and I'm worried

67
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:33,770
罗布穿短裤会显得不礼貌
it's going to look disrespectful if Rob wears shorts.

68
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:36,550
亲爱的 外面可有13度 我才不要穿长裤
Honey, it's 55 degrees out. I'm not wearing long pants.

69
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:38,050
没事的 那是好莱坞
You're fine. It's Hollywood.

70
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:40,240
还有人不穿裤子在那逛呢
There'll be people there with no pants.

71
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:40,880
你好 莉莉
Hi, Lily.

72
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:42,330
莉莉 跟蒙蒂打个招呼
Lily, say hi to Monte.

73
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:43,930
你好
Hi.

74
00:02:45,350 --> 00:02:47,730
不好意思 她从来没这么害羞过
I'm...sorry. She's never this shy.

75
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:50,230
不 我们才不好意思 好像什么吓着她了
No, we'sorry. Seems like something scared her.

76
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:57,910
太有爱了
It was adorable.

77
00:02:57,910 --> 00:03:01,070
莉莉很明显被加拿大的小蒙蒂迷住了
Lily was clearly smitten with that little Canadian Monte.

78
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:03,030
听出来歧视了 不好意思
Just heard that. Delightful.

79
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:06,020
这是我一直以来期待的成长里程碑
It was a rite of passage that I had been looking forward to --

80
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:08,070
我女儿的初恋
My daughter's first crush.

81
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:09,630
我想去支持帮助她
And I wanted to be there for her

82
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,410
因为当年没有人支持帮助我
in a way that no one was there for me.

83
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:14,200
也难怪 我的初恋是法院前
Of course, my first crush was on a statue

84
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:16,740
一座联邦政府将军的雕塑
of a confederate general in front of a courthouse.

85
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,550
也是在那一年他们挂上了
That's the same year they put up

86
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:20,630
"严禁攀爬"的牌子
The "Do Not Climb The Statue" signs.

87
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:24,850
抱歉来晚了
Sorry I'm late.

88
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:27,330
这衣服可以吗 车里还有另一件
Is this shirt okay? I got another one in the car.

89
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:29,110
只不过是吃顿午餐 淡定点
It's just lunch. Calm down.

90
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:31,020
你男友会喜欢的
Your boyfriend's gonna love it.

91
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,520
去年夏天 我和菲尔在卡波待了五天
Last summer, Phil and I went to Cabo for five days,

92
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,840
认识了汤姆和丽萨·德兰尼夫妇 玩得超开心
and we met Tom and Lisa Delaney, and we had so much fun,

93
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,010
每次他们过来我们都一定会跟他们聚会
we make sure to see them every time they're in town.

94
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:41,360
汤姆是一位十分成功的投资银行家
Tom's a hugely successful investment banker.

95
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,900
他参与很多的慈善活动
He does tons of charity work,

96
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,450
他能3小时24分跑完全程马拉松
he runs a marathon in 3:24,

97
00:03:44,450 --> 00:03:46,060
他还会开自己的直升机
and he flies his own helicopter.

98
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,650
是啊 而丽萨呢
Yeah, and Lisa...

99
00:03:47,650 --> 00:03:49,910
丽萨可真是个幸运的女士
Yeah, she is one lucky lady.

100
00:03:50,490 --> 00:03:51,880
他们来之前
Before they get here,

101
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:54,270
你能不能答应我不要付账
can you promise me you won't pick up the check?

102
00:03:54,270 --> 00:03:55,450
为什么
Why?

103
00:03:55,810 --> 00:03:57,350
亲爱的 我喜欢他们
Oh, honey, I like them,

104
00:03:57,350 --> 00:03:59,670
卡波之行后我们见了他们三次
but we've seen them three times since Cabo.

105
00:03:59,670 --> 00:04:02,670
每次他们都会点最贵的东西
Every time, they order the most expensive stuff.

106
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:04,780
他们是我们认识最有钱的人
They are the richest people we know --

107
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,680
谢谢
Thank you.

108
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:09,110
然而我从来没见过他伸手去够账单
And yet I have not seen him reach for the check once.

109
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:11,050
汤姆不方便伸手够东西
Tom has trouble reaching for stuff.

110
00:04:11,050 --> 00:04:13,060
他上大学投棒球伤了肩膀
He hurt his shoulder pitching in college.

111
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,160
NCAA第一分区
Division 1.

112
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,900
你之所以急着去付账
You feel a need to pick up the check

113
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,210
是因为你敬畏他
because you're intimidated by him

114
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:18,210
想要证明些什么
and you want to prove something.

115
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:20,710
怎么可能 我只不过嫌账单碍眼
That's crazy. I just don't like it when the bill sits there.

116
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,370
太尴尬了
It's awkward.

117
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:22,760
你不能一不喜欢什么东西
You can't just roll over on something

118
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,100
就往那东西上面摸啊
'cause it makes you feel uncomfortable.

119
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:25,190
随你便吧
Whatever you want.

120
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,770
美人你好啊
Hello, beautiful.

121
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:27,900
帅哥你好
Hi, handsome.

122
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,930
你们好啊
Hey, you two.

123
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:38,600
天啊 见到你们太高兴了
Hi! Oh, my gosh. It is so great to see you guys.

124
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,880
开瓶香槟吧
Let's get some champagne.

125
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,510
开吧
Let's do it.

126
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,120
我受够了
Okay, that's it.

127
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:48,210
如果你们那么讨厌它 就直说吧
If you hate it so much, just tell me.

128
00:04:48,210 --> 00:04:49,980
好吧 你的古龙水糟透了
Fine. Your cologne is horrible.

129
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,810
你闻起来就好像脱衣女郎死在包厢里
You smell like a stripper died in a cabin.

130
00:04:51,810 --> 00:04:53,820
我没在说古龙水
I'm not talking about my cologne.

131
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:56,970
这就是为何我会按兵不动等他自己说
That's why I hang back and wait for him to get specific.

132
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:58,250
我的胡子
My mustache.

133
00:04:58,250 --> 00:04:59,540
我都留了好几周了
I've been growing it for weeks,

134
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:02,090
而你们俩安静得有点可疑
and the two of you have been conspicuously silent.

135
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:03,200
很好看
It's very dashing.

136
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:04,460
什么胡子
What mustache?

137
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,090
好吧 杰 好像我会相信你没看到似的
Right, Jay. Like I'm supposed to believe you didn't see it.

138
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:08,020
你赢了
You got me.

139
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,520
待会儿见 塞尔皮科
Check you later, Serpico.

140
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,950
塞尔皮科
Serpico!

141
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:13,530
你连那是谁都不知道
You don't even know who that is.

142
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,010
杰
Jay.

143
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:17,200
你拿着高尔夫球杆要去干什么
Where are you going with your golf clubs?

144
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,630
去黑夜中击球
Take a shot in the dark.

145
00:05:18,630 --> 00:05:20,230
可我们约了玩伴啊
But we have a playdate.

146
00:05:20,230 --> 00:05:22,030
真的吗 昨晚不是才玩过吗
Really? We just had one last night.

147
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,000
不是我不答应
Not that I'm saying no --

148
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,080
但今天这个节奏有点不太对啊
Just quicker turnaround than usual.

149
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,020
给乔约的玩伴
A playdate for Joe.

150
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:29,110
他父母都要来 所以你得在场
And both parents are coming, so you have to be here.

151
00:05:29,110 --> 00:05:30,710
你在开玩笑吧
You've got to be kidding me.

152
00:05:30,710 --> 00:05:32,480
这年头孩子们得预约
I mean, it's bad enough that these kids today

153
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,060
才能和别人玩已经够惨了
have to make a date to play with each other.

154
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,860
他们不能到大街上去踢铁罐
They can't go in the street and kick a can

155
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:38,390
或对着朋友杂志插页上的金·诺瓦克流口水
Or drool over a friend's centerfold of Kim Novak.

156
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:40,120
说点我能懂的好吗
Say something I understand.

157
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:43,120
我们为什么要坐在一旁看孩子玩呢
Why do we all have to sit around and watch our kids play?

158
00:05:43,130 --> 00:05:45,150
因为大家现在都是这么做的
Because that's what people do now.

159
00:05:45,150 --> 00:05:46,850
而且乔对此非常高兴呢
And Joe is very excited about it.

160
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:48,550
第一个真人朋友
His first real friend.

161
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:50,630
-歌洛莉亚 -怎么不行了
- Gloria... - What's the problem?

162
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:52,390
我很喜欢那个妈妈 而且大家都说
I like the mom, and everybody says

163
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,780
你和那爸爸有很多共同点
that you and the dad have a lot in common.

164
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,190
会很有趣的
It's going to be fun.

165
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,870
快请进 各位
Come in, everybody.

166
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,920
歌洛莉亚 这是我丈夫 马蒂
Gloria, this is my husband, Marty.

167
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,410
瞧瞧你啊
Look at you.

168
00:06:06,410 --> 00:06:07,770
美得像一幅画
Pretty as a pinup.

169
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:10,490
那位传说中的幸运老公在哪儿呢
And where's the lucky husband I've been hearing about?

170
00:06:10,490 --> 00:06:12,350
马蒂 那是杰
Marty, that's Jay.

171
00:06:12,570 --> 00:06:14,400
真好 你的确也很老
Oh, good. You are old.

172
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,990
我还怕他们夸大其词了呢
I was scared they were exaggerating.

173
00:06:19,810 --> 00:06:23,370
我可不想提前剧透
Um, so...I don't want to spoil any surprises,

174
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:25,180
不过 如果让你猜的话
But, uh, if you had to guess,

175
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,380
你觉得我们今天是要去干嘛呢
What -- what would you say we're doing today?

176
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:30,270
对 看看你能不能猜中我们的计划
Yeah, let's just see if you pick what we have planned.

177
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:31,390
我想想啊
Let's see.

178
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,220
天啊
Oh, my god.

179
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,500
是那个在奥克斯纳德的农场吗
Is it that farm in Oxnard

180
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:36,370
我 小卡和莉莉一起去摘草莓的那个地方
where Cam and Lily and I went strawberry-picking?

181
00:06:36,470 --> 00:06:38,170
我们度过了最棒的
We had the most wonderful --

182
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:41,850
抱歉 不过你真的太会猜了
Sorry, but you are just so great at this game.

183
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,580
可是现在不是草莓的季节 所以肯定不是那
But it's not strawberry season, so it can't be that.

184
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:48,220
这也是为何我们没选那里
Which is exactly why we didn't pick that.

185
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,990
那再猜
Okay, so...guess again.

186
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,490
等等 我好像闻到了海水的味道
Wait -- do I smell the ocean?

187
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:54,200
你们是要带我去沙滩上那家超赞的卡尔顿酒店吗
Are you taking me to that fabulous Carlton's on the beach?

188
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,200
那儿有最
They have the most --

189
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,740
我们可没说一定是哦
Well, we're not making any promises,

190
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:00,460
不过这猜测挺靠谱的
but that would be a pretty good guess.

191
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,510
如果他们没有停业整修的话
If they weren't closed for renovations.

192
00:07:02,510 --> 00:07:04,310
该死 继续想 米奇尔舅舅
Damn it! Think, Uncle Mitchell.

193
00:07:04,310 --> 00:07:05,350
好像有点热了
It's getting a little warm in here.

194
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,100
你们介意开个车窗[打碎玻璃]吗
Do you mind if we crack a window?

195
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:08,910
除非我已经用头把它撞开了
Unless I've already done that with my head.

196
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,750
我们要停下来加油
We -- we need to stop for gas, okay?

197
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:12,460
别摘眼罩 米奇尔舅舅
Just keep your blindfold on, Uncle Mitchell.

198
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,200
好吧
Okay.

199
00:07:13,930 --> 00:07:15,340
行 行吧
Fine. This is fine.

200
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,360
加满油
Fill 'er up!

201
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,410
好的 女士
Yes, Ma'am.

202
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:19,610
开玩笑吧
Seriously?

203
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,460
这样一直开着车乱转也不是办法
We can't just keep driving around.

204
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,890
我们得去个什么地方
We need to go somewhere.

205
00:07:24,890 --> 00:07:26,810
集中精力 各位 米奇尔舅舅喜欢什么
Focus, people. What does Uncle Mitchell like?

206
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:28,150
不知道 基佬相关的 对吧
I don't know. Gay things, right?

207
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,740
你们能想到的最基的东西是啥
What's the gayest thing you can think of?

208
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,020
他的结婚对象
He's married to it.

209
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:31,980
快看
Hey, look.

210
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,470
每个人都爱追星 我们可以带他去星房观光
Everybody loves stars. We could take him on a tour.

211
00:07:36,470 --> 00:07:37,770
开车转悠 到处看看房子
Driving around looking at houses

212
00:07:37,770 --> 00:07:39,670
可算不上什么生日欢乐
isn't much of a birthday fun day?

213
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,050
我们需要更多时间
We need more time.

214
00:07:41,930 --> 00:07:43,290
先把他敲晕吧
Let's knock him out.

215
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,170
查理兹·塞隆 哈里森·福特 哈莉·贝瑞
Charlize Theron, Harrison Ford, Halle Berry...

216
00:07:52,170 --> 00:07:53,860
这些听起来都不是他的菜
None of these seem very Uncle Mitchell.

217
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,020
米奇尔舅舅喜欢什么呢
What does Uncle Mitchell like?

218
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:56,170
基佬的事物
Gay things.

219
00:07:56,170 --> 00:07:57,630
那这个就是基王争霸赛里的霸主了
Then here's the mother lode.

220
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,930
芭芭拉·史翠珊[著名艺人] 太赞了
Barbra Streisand! Perfect!

221
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:00,900
等等 等等 等等
Okay, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

222
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,260
我们怎么知道这地图是不是真的
How do we know these maps are real?

223
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,490
你以为我拿些假地图来干这事业吗
You think I built this whole business on fake maps?

224
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,130
什么事业 你只有一块招牌和一张草坪躺椅
What business? You got a sign and a lawn chair.

225
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:09,280
我们可以抓紧吗 我可能还有只猫要喂
Can we wrap this up? I might still have a cat to feed.

226
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:13,550
菲尔估计拍了一百张我的沙滩照吧
Phil must have taken 100 pictures of me on the beach

227
00:08:13,550 --> 00:08:16,320
就为了拍到我后面的裸女
just to get one shot of the topless women behind me.

228
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,000
你后面有裸女吗
There were topless women behind you?

229
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:21,200
账单放这了 你们准备买单叫我就好
Here you go. I'll just take this when you're ready.

230
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,900
好 谢谢
Oh, okay. Thank you.

231
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:27,670
你们今天还有什么安排吗
So, what do you two have planned for the rest of today?

232
00:08:27,670 --> 00:08:29,190
没什么安排 真的
Nothing...really.

233
00:08:29,190 --> 00:08:30,870
但如果你们要走了 这
But if you need to wind it up, it's --

234
00:08:30,870 --> 00:08:32,600
不 我们不急
Nah. We're good.

235
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,920
那好 好
Yeah, good. Good.

236
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:37,970
你们呢 有计划什么好玩的吗 还是
Do you guys, uh, you have any fun trips planned or...

237
00:08:37,970 --> 00:08:40,110
我计划着去趟卫生间
Well, I was planning on visiting the restroom,

238
00:08:40,110 --> 00:08:42,500
顺利的话 可能犹如西班牙四月的雨季
and if all goes well, then maybe Spain in April.

239
00:08:42,770 --> 00:08:44,010
再会 朋友
Adios, amigo.

240
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:46,440
与上帝同在
I vaya con dios!

241
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,740
管住你的手 朋友
You want to keep that hand, amigo?

242
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,690
法国真的太美了
And France was just beautiful.

243
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,500
自从诺曼底登陆日后我就没去过了
I hadn't been there since D-Day.

244
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,870
尽管再次走过那片沙滩
Took me the same amount of time

245
00:08:54,870 --> 00:08:56,970
还是花了我那么久的时间
to get across that beach, though.

246
00:08:57,430 --> 00:08:58,820
你也参过军吧
You were in the service?

247
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:00,070
有 不过是不同战争
Yeah, but different war.

248
00:09:00,070 --> 00:09:01,230
和北朝鲜那次吧 我也参加了
Oh, Korea. Me too.

249
00:09:01,230 --> 00:09:02,880
不 是下一场[越战] 继续猜
No, next war. Keep going.

250
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:05,050
谁要吃奶酪呢
Anybody want some cheese?

251
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:08,130
我吃不了 心血管不太好
Not me. Gums up the old ticker.

252
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:09,440
杰懂的
Jay knows about that.

253
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,690
不懂 我可爱吃奶酪了
No idea. Love the stuff.

254
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:11,970
吃杏仁小心点
Just be careful with the almonds.

255
00:09:11,970 --> 00:09:13,220
不然假牙可能会咬坏掉
You may break the denture.

256
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,320
我这不是假牙 是种植牙
Uh, it's not a denture. It's an implant.

257
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,750
这个我们都说过几次了
How many times have we been over this?

258
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,190
你也容易忘东忘西 对吧
You forget stuff, too, huh?

259
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:19,410
我从来不健忘
I never forget anything.

260
00:09:19,410 --> 00:09:21,790
在商场停车 我们还要拍张照记下位置
When we park at the mall, we have to take a picture.

261
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:24,140
杰 歌洛莉亚说你上一段婚姻也有孩子
Jay, Gloria tells me you have kids from your first marriage.

262
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:25,260
马蒂也是
So does Marty.

263
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:28,310
是啊 我最大的孩子有66岁
Yeah. My oldest is, uh, 66.

264
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,850
她去年去世了
Was. She passed last year.

265
00:09:30,850 --> 00:09:31,840
我很遗憾
Oh, I'm so sorry.

266
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,080
那还年轻 怎么去世的
Well, that's young. What was it?

267
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,300
自然过世的
Natural causes.

268
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:36,400
我觉得都要怪压力过大
I blame most of it on stress.

269
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:39,300
现在的压力比过去大多了
So much more pressure than there was years ago.

270
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:40,120
回想我们那年代
Back in our day --

271
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,670
不同年代 我们不是一个年代
Different day. Not the same day.

272
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,190
事实上跟你去世的女儿差不多年代
Actually more your dead daughter's day.

273
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:44,640
愿她安息
May she rest in peace.

274
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,050
老妈 我们得谈谈
Mom, we need to talk.

275
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:49,790
你在这干嘛呢
What are you doing here?

276
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:51,420
你应该在上面看孩子的
You're supposed to be watching the kids.

277
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:53,590
韦斯利对乔会有不良影响的
Wesley is a bad influence on joe.

278
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:55,100
他很粗鲁又没礼貌
He's rude and disrespectful,

279
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:57,000
而且我觉得你得趁早扼杀了这段友情
and I think you should nip this friendship in the bud.

280
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,900
他取笑你的胡子 对吧
He made fun of your mustache, didn't he?

281
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:01,250
哪有四岁小孩还会知道"稀疏"这词
What kind of 4-year-old knows the word "Wispy"?

282
00:10:01,990 --> 00:10:04,200
曼尼 看着我
Manny, look at me.

283
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:08,510
都这么近了 我还是没看到他胡子
This close, and I still couldn't see it.

284
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:10,630
再留久一点吧 好吗
It's just for a little while longer, okay?

285
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:11,470
好吧
Fine.

286
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:15,680
但是如果他们惹我的话 我也不会放过他们
But if they mess with me, I'm gonna mess with them.

287
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:20,480
你每天晚上要起来尿几次
How many times a night do you have to get up to pee?

288
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:21,820
我差不多四五次
I'm up to four or five.

289
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:24,030
我可不用 老前辈 最多两次
Not me, old-timer. Twice tops.

290
00:10:24,030 --> 00:10:25,510
上个月有一次 我一整晚都没起过夜
Once last month, I even slept through the night.

291
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:26,780
我现在要去喝酒了
Now, I'm gonna refresh this

292
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,600
因为我没什么好担心的
'cause I got nothing to worry about.

293
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:31,700
我竟然真的跟那个混蛋
I'm literally in a pissing contest

294
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:33,260
在比尿尿次数
with the son of a bitch.

295
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,650
为什么我们要用上等的瓷器用餐呢
Why are we eating off the good china?

296
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:38,030
因为我们午餐有客人
Because we're having company for lunch.

297
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:39,100
谁要来啊
Who's coming?

298
00:10:39,690 --> 00:10:42,810
好吧 我邀请了楼上的蒙蒂和他家人
Okay, I invited Monte and his family from upstairs.

299
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:44,280
什么 为什么
What?! Why?!

300
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:47,330
因为当爸爸的看出他女儿对人动心了呀
Because a daddy can tell when his little girl has a crush.

301
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:48,570
我不知道你在讲什么
I don't know what you're talking about.

302
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:49,800
莉莉 你要去哪儿
Hey, Lily, where are you going?

303
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,610
我希望你能放心地跟我聊这些
Look, I want you to be able to talk to me

304
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:52,930
感情这类的事情
about this kind of stuff.

305
00:10:52,930 --> 00:10:54,730
对别人有感觉
It's completely natural and healthy

306
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:56,990
是很自然也很健康的
to have feelings for someone.

307
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,890
而且你知道吗 我觉得他也喜欢你
And you know what? I think he likes you, too.

308
00:10:59,970 --> 00:11:01,070
你只要勾他一下 懂吗
You just have to draw him out, you know?

309
00:11:01,070 --> 00:11:02,840
-稍微挑逗下 -怎么做
- Flirt a little. - How?

310
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,400
你就坐到他面前
Uh, well, you just sit down in front of him,

311
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:07,050
望着他的双眼 甜甜地笑上一个
look him straight in the eye, put a big smile on your face,

312
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:08,290
再问他些问题
and ask him some questions,

313
00:11:08,290 --> 00:11:10,110
比如 你有什么兴趣爱好吗
like, "So, do you have any hobbies?

314
00:11:10,730 --> 00:11:13,390
加拿大真有人们说的那么美吗
Is Canada really as beautiful as they say it is?

315
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:15,590
你喜欢培根吗
Are you a fan of the bacon?"

316
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:17,870
你干嘛要那样眨眼
Why are you blinking like that?

317
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:19,590
因为我要给他传递信号啊
Well, because I'm sending him signals.

318
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:20,300
还有什么呢
Okay, what else?

319
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,500
一定要称赞他的着装
Definitely compliment him on his outfit,

320
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,590
他讲笑话一定要笑
laugh at his jokes.

321
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:24,900
如果笑话不好笑呢
What if they aren't funny?

322
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:26,530
宝贝儿 撒了笑料就不是鲜肉了
Oh, honey, the cute ones rarely are.

323
00:11:26,530 --> 00:11:28,310
上帝可不会什么都赋予
God doesn't give with both hands.

324
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:31,510
可不要乐出心脏病来
Okay, do not have a heart attack,

325
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:33,330
当你摘下眼罩时
but when you take off your blindfold,

326
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:35,340
你将看到的不是别人
you will be standing in front of none other

327
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:38,880
而正是传奇巨星
than the legendary superstar...

328
00:11:38,890 --> 00:11:40,780
-谁 -大名鼎鼎的
- Who? - the one and only...

329
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,470
-谁 -芭芭拉·史翠珊
- Who? - Ms. Barbra Streisand--

330
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:43,500
我的天
Oh, my!

331
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,770
的家
's house.

332
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:47,550
你们当真吗 她真住这里吗
Oh, are you serious? She actually lives here?

333
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:49,730
难以置信
I can't believe it.

334
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,560
快瞧 她家大门开了
Dude, look. Her gate is open.

335
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:53,270
我们应该给你在她家车道上照张相
We should get a picture of you in her driveway.

336
00:11:53,270 --> 00:11:55,350
这样的生日礼物岂不是赞上天了
How awesome of a birthday fun day gift would that be?

337
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,280
这样的话 胡娇绝对嫉妒死了
Okay. You know what? Pepper would die.

338
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,750
他为了《燕特尔》给自己办了第二次犹太受戒礼
He loved "Yentl" so much, he had a second Bar Mitzvah.

339
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:01,500
来照吧
Okay, let's -- let's do it.

340
00:12:01,510 --> 00:12:02,650
站到房子前面
Okay, right in front of the house.

341
00:12:02,650 --> 00:12:04,180
棒极了
Yeah. This is fantastic.

342
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:05,870
*胡娇 你听到了吗*
*Pepper, can you hear me?*

343
00:12:05,870 --> 00:12:07,390
*胡娇 你看到了吗*
*Pepper, can you see me?*

344
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:09,680
*胡娇 我站在车道上*
*Pepper, I am standing in the driveway*

345
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:11,140
不好意思 你们在干什么
Excuse me. Can I help you?

346
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,570
实在抱歉 我们刚刚在
I'm so sorry. We were just --

347
00:12:13,010 --> 00:12:14,820
天啊 你是雷·利奥塔[美国演员]
Oh, my god. You're Ray Liotta.

348
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:16,590
他真是她的大粉丝诶
He really is a big fan.

349
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:18,470
连她园丁的名字都知道
He even knows the name of her gardener.

350
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,690
《好家伙》[90年电影]
"Goodfellas"?

351
00:12:21,690 --> 00:12:22,860
《散弹露露》[90年电影]
"Something Wild"?

352
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:24,430
《梦幻成真》[89年电影]
"Field of dreams"?

353
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,520
-没看过 -那年头我们都还没出生呢
- Never seen it. - Okay, we're really not that old.

354
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,610
雷·利奥塔是一位很好的演员
Look, Ray Liotta is a very fine actor,

355
00:12:28,610 --> 00:12:30,590
我们占用了他太多的时间
And we have taken up enough of his time.

356
00:12:30,590 --> 00:12:31,680
别不停地重复我的全名
Stop saying my full name

357
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,320
搞得好像你不提他们就不知道我是谁似的
like you have to keep telling them who I am.

358
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,350
等等 你和芭芭拉·史翠珊住一起吗
So, wait -- you live with Barbra Streisand?

359
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,530
你有地图吧
Y-y-you got the map.

360
00:12:38,530 --> 00:12:41,540
她十五年前在这里住过两个月
She lived here for about 2 months 15 years ago.

361
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,870
你觉得那些混蛋会更新这些玩意儿
You think the bastards would update these things

362
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:46,550
显示目前住在这里的影星是谁吗
to reflect the current movie-star owners.

363
00:12:46,550 --> 00:12:47,520
谢谢 走吧 孩子们
Thank you. Come on, kids.

364
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,380
很抱歉打扰了您
We're very sorry to have bothered you.

365
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:51,060
不 不 我不想你们空手而归
No, no, no. I don't want you to leave empty-handed.

366
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,180
过来拍张自拍吧
Come on in for a selfie.

367
00:12:52,370 --> 00:12:54,530
好吧 给你
All right. Um... Here. O-okay.

368
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,060
等你们看过我的电影之后
When you see my movies later,

369
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,590
就会意识到这可是个特殊的时刻
you're gonna realize that this is a special moment.

370
00:12:58,590 --> 00:13:01,290
来吧 茄子
Come on. And "Cheeeeese"!

371
00:13:01,290 --> 00:13:03,580
看到没 这可是老演员微笑的秘诀
See? That's an old actor's trick for a perfect smile.

372
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:05,620
只不过只有我和你在笑 你们都没笑
Except you and I are smiling. You guys aren't smiling.

373
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:06,750
怎么一回事
W-what's the matter?

374
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,190
不是你的问题 利奥塔先生
It's not you, Mr. Liotta.

375
00:13:08,190 --> 00:13:10,550
我们只是觉得让自己的舅舅失望了
We just really feel like we let our uncle down.

376
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:13,730
我们本应给他准备一个特殊的生日
We were supposed to plan a special day for his birthday,

377
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,280
可我们彻底失败了
and we totally flaked.

378
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:15,920
我们真的很抱歉
We're so sorry.

379
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,320
我们想了很久到底该把你带去哪里
We tried to figure out where to take you,

380
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:20,030
也知道你有多么地喜欢芭芭拉·史翠珊
and we know how much you love Barbra Streisand.

381
00:13:20,030 --> 00:13:22,600
你总是送给我们最棒的礼物
You always give us the most awesome gifts.

382
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,390
我们逊毙了
We suck.

383
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:24,560
别这么说
Don't say that.

384
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:26,140
煎蛋卷舞到第二段时
I kind of figured you didn't have anything

385
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,840
我就大概知道你们什么都没准备了
by the second verse of the omelet dance.

386
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,110
我可是零基础
Hey, I've had no training.

387
00:13:29,110 --> 00:13:31,530
但当我看到你们为了让我开心而那么卖力时
But then I saw how hard you were trying to make me happy,

388
00:13:31,530 --> 00:13:34,550
我真的是很喜欢和你们在一起
and I just love hanging out with you guys.

389
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:38,020
再说了 我还见到了雷·利奥 雷
Plus, I did get to meet Ray Lio-- Ray.

390
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:40,240
你也会见到芭芭拉的
You're also gonna meet Barbra.

391
00:13:40,430 --> 00:13:41,340
开什么玩笑
What? No.

392
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,180
我本来也要去她家一趟的
I've been meaning to go by her house anyway.

393
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,310
我这儿有一堆她的邮件
I've got a bunch of her mail.

394
00:13:44,310 --> 00:13:45,450
不用这么麻烦你了
Oh, you don't have to do that.

395
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:46,750
不 不 不
No, no, no, no.

396
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:47,660
你让我想起了
You remind me of --

397
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,240
我小时候爱着的一个人
of someone that I loved when I was a kid.

398
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,780
我也有个逗逼舅舅
I had a funny uncle, too.

399
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,690
你真是太热情了
This is so nice of you.

400
00:13:54,690 --> 00:13:55,620
我得承认
Well, I must admit,

401
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:58,210
请你们来其实是有点自己的小打算
I-I have a little bit of an ulterior motive.

402
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:01,390
我觉得莉莉看上你们家那个了
I think Lily has a giant crush on your little guy.

403
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,530
我有点想给他们牵红线
I kind of wanted to set them up.

404
00:14:02,530 --> 00:14:04,750
我这人特别喜欢搞浪漫
I know -- I'm a hopeless romantic.

405
00:14:05,130 --> 00:14:06,160
太有爱了
Oh! That's so cute!

406
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,770
我还记得我的初恋 那是在夏令营
I remember my first crush. It was at summer camp.

407
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:10,400
我住在多伦多 他是埃德蒙顿来的
I lived in Toronto, and he was from Edmonton,

408
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,030
也算是有缘无分
So it was very star-crossed.

409
00:14:12,030 --> 00:14:14,150
有点像我们的小罗密欧与朱丽叶
Just like our little Romeo and Juliet.

410
00:14:14,150 --> 00:14:15,970
他是我爱过的第一个男孩
He was the first boy I ever loved.

411
00:14:16,110 --> 00:14:17,500
比利·麦克林
Billy Macklin.

412
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:20,150
天啊 我都多少年没想起过他了
God. I haven't thought of him in years.

413
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,680
你有什么兴趣爱好吗
Do you have any hobbies?

414
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,110
我喜欢攀岩
Well, I like rock climbing.

415
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:24,080
我收集宠物小精灵
I collect Pokemon --

416
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,870
我听说加拿大挺不错
I hear Canada's nice.

417
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:26,740
你喜欢培根吗
Do you like bacon?

418
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:27,740
话说起来 我要去
Okay, you know what, I'm just gonna --

419
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:29,660
夏天一过就开始出现问题了
After that summer, things got pretty rough.

420
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,570
爹死了 娘也开始酗酒
Dad died, Mom started drinking.

421
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,160
太难承受了
It was a lot to handle.

422
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:35,390
我喜欢你的衬衫 是新的吗
I love your shirt. Is it new?

423
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:37,700
我想这衬衫的年岁比你还大
Oh, I think this shirt's older than you are.

424
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,290
莉莉 到卧室去 跟你有话说
Okay, Lily, can I see you in the bedroom, please?

425
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:44,220
比我还大 罗布 你可笑死我了
Older than I am -- oh, Rob, you're killing me!

426
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,680
我们去去就回
Okay, we'll be right back.

427
00:14:46,110 --> 00:14:47,490
别骚了
And enough.

428
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:50,420
你刚才在干什么
What are you doing out there?

429
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:51,540
你教我的啊
What you told me.

430
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,390
我觉得进展不错
I think it's going pretty good.

431
00:14:53,390 --> 00:14:55,370
我还以为你看上的是蒙蒂
I thought your crush was on Monte.

432
00:14:55,370 --> 00:14:57,190
你不能和成年人调情啊
You can't flirt with a grown man.

433
00:14:57,190 --> 00:14:57,820
可你说过
But you said --

434
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,660
不 这样不好
No. It's not appropriate.

435
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:02,280
不 我再也不要和男生说话了
Oh, no! I'm never talking to a boy ever again!

436
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:05,200
莉莉 你没必要感到羞愧
Lily, you have nothing to be ashamed of.

437
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,850
要怪就怪我吧
If -- if anything, this is -- this is my fault.

438
00:15:07,850 --> 00:15:10,490
我还以为你喜欢蒙蒂 是我的错
I thought you meant Monte, and I confused you.

439
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,350
我能告诉你个秘密吗
Can I...tell you a little secret?

440
00:15:14,350 --> 00:15:15,310
不
No!

441
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:17,970
当我对初恋采取行动时
Well, when I made a move on my first crush,

442
00:15:17,970 --> 00:15:18,920
情况完全失控了
it went way worse.

443
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:22,280
那天是新年前夜 我跑去给他一个吻
It was New Year's Eve, and I went to give him a kiss,

444
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:24,290
结果舌头黏在他脸上了
and my tongue froze to his cheek.

445
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:27,440
为什么冻上了
Why did it freeze?

446
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:29,000
天太冷 而且他还是铜做的
It was cold, and he was made out of bronze,

447
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,280
我再也不想说这事儿了
And I don't want to talk about this anymore.

448
00:15:33,290 --> 00:15:34,230
你在干什么
What are you doing?

449
00:15:34,230 --> 00:15:36,830
马蒂说我们这年纪的人做不了十个仰卧起坐
Marty said guys our age can't do 10 sit-ups.

450
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,740
我不记得说过这话 但像是我说的话
I don't remember saying it, but it sounds like me.

451
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:41,420
杰 麻烦你过来一下
Jay, may I speak with you for a moment?

452
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:42,440
好
All right.

453
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:46,840
糟了
Ah, crap!

454
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,510
让我帮你
Uh, here. L-let me help you.

455
00:15:48,770 --> 00:15:49,990
我要倒了
I'm going down!

456
00:15:50,030 --> 00:15:51,420
维琪
Vicky!

457
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,490
你今天是怎么回事
What is wrong with you today?

458
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:55,950
我受够了马蒂把我
I'm sick of Marty lumping me

459
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,860
跟他们一个年龄段的人混为一谈
into the same age category as him.

460
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:59,250
说什么 像我们这样的人 我们那时候
"Guys like us," "Back in our day."

461
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,080
我可是战后婴儿潮出生的人
I'm a baby boomer, for god's sake.

462
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,440
我记得《点燃我的火》[60年代金曲]全部歌词
I know all the words to "Light My Fire."

463
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,710
杰 你不能只再为自己着想了
Jay, you have to stop thinking only about you.

464
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:07,310
我知道 我改为乔着想
Yeah, I know, I know. I should think about Joe.

465
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:08,900
不 为我
No -- Me!

466
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,100
你知道我和维琪
Do you know that Vicky and I

467
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:13,550
是班上年纪最大的妈妈吗 比别人大得多
are the oldest moms in the class -- by a lot?

468
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:14,090
所以呢
So?

469
00:16:14,090 --> 00:16:15,070
你也许不知道
This might surprise you,

470
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:18,130
变老对女人也是件烦心事
but aging is also a big deal for women.

471
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,660
我需要维琪做我的朋友
I need Vicky to be my friend.

472
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,770
在那群年轻妈妈里我觉得很不自在
I feel out of place around all those young moms.

473
00:16:22,770 --> 00:16:24,130
如果你不喜欢她老公
And if you don't like her husband,

474
00:16:24,130 --> 00:16:25,720
也许她就不喜欢我了
maybe she'll stop liking me.

475
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:26,790
歌洛莉亚 我在努力 但是
Gloria, I'm trying, but it's --

476
00:16:26,790 --> 00:16:29,530
至少你不是最老的爸爸
At least you're not the oldest dad.

477
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:30,990
你就不能享受这一点吗
Can't you enjoy that?

478
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,030
上一次你作为
When was the last time

479
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:34,680
年轻人亮相是什么时候
that you were the young stud in the room?

480
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:36,740
我把我妈送进养老院那回
When I put Mom in that nursing home.

481
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:37,830
就那么一小会儿
That was quite a rush.

482
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,080
你能更友善一点吗
So, are you going to be nice?

483
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,620
好 他也没那么差啦
Yes. He's not a bad guy.

484
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:41,930
再说啦 我要忍他的日子
And really, how much longer

485
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:43,400
也没剩多少了
am I gonna have to put up with him?

486
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:44,880
不 杰 不准这么说
Ay, no, Jay. Don't say that.

487
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,390
你会很长寿的
You're going to live a long life.

488
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:48,460
不是我 我说的是外面那老头
Not me! Grandpa out there!

489
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:49,470
他能听见
He can hear you.

490
00:16:49,470 --> 00:16:50,380
听见什么
Hear what?

491
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,370
你们又在谈论我的胡子吗
You were talking about my mustache again?

492
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:54,100
不 曼尼 我们喜欢你的胡子
No, Manny. We love your mustache.

493
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:55,040
搞笑
Oh, hilarious.

494
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:57,270
我把胡子都剃了你说你喜欢
Tell me you like it now that I've shaved it off!

495
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:01,110
母亲是黑人 父亲是白人 但我没见过他
Black mother and white father, but I've never met him.

496
00:17:01,510 --> 00:17:02,950
这才是社会上该流传的故事
That's a story that should be out there more --

497
00:17:02,950 --> 00:17:05,030
白人父亲抛妻弃子[一般是黑人父亲]
White fathers who abandon their families.

498
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:07,150
还有什么 还有什么
What else? What else?

499
00:17:07,150 --> 00:17:09,440
这位是沃尔特
So, this is Walter.

500
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:12,010
就好像我之前接杰罗米的班一样
Just as I took over for Jeremy when his shift ended,

501
00:17:12,210 --> 00:17:13,840
他要来接我的班了
he'll be taking over for me.

502
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:14,900
或者说你们准备好买单了
Unless you're ready?

503
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:18,020
我觉得我们还得聊会儿 谢啦
I think we're still talking. But thanks.

504
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:20,580
沃尔特 我能到那边问你个问题吗
Walter? Could I ask you a quick question right over there?

505
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,580
我也马上就回来
I'll be right back, too.

506
00:17:22,830 --> 00:17:24,850
我需要跟我老公聊两句 谢谢
I just need a minute alone with my husband. Thank you.

507
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:27,480
这单绝对不能由你来付
There is no way you are paying that bill.

508
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:28,740
放在那儿都多久了
It has been out there forever,

509
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:30,910
他手都没往钱包上伸过 装都不装一下
and he hasn't even pretended to reach for his wallet.

510
00:17:30,910 --> 00:17:31,930
太折磨人了 克莱尔
This is torture, Claire.

511
00:17:31,930 --> 00:17:33,360
我愿意付任何账结束这一切
I'll pay anything to end it.

512
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,470
挺住
Stay strong.

513
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:37,020
我挺不住 你嫁给了一个挺不住的男人
I'm weak. You married a weak man!

514
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,340
把卡给我 把卡
Give it to me. Give it --

515
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:38,940
菲尔
Phil --

516
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:42,140
不 沃特尔 沃特尔
No! Walter! Walter!

517
00:17:42,150 --> 00:17:44,230
沃特尔 不
Walter! D'ohh!

518
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,260
好吧 我说开了吧
Okay. Here's the thing.

519
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,700
-我喜欢和你们 -不 克莱尔 不
- We like hanging out -- - No, Claire! No!

520
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:48,880
我知道是怎么一回事
I know what this is about.

521
00:17:48,890 --> 00:17:51,110
汤姆 你该把账付了 太没礼貌了
Tom, you should have paid the check. It's rude.

522
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:53,270
他没有不礼貌 他很好 是我必须付账
He's not rude. He's wonderful. I had to pay.

523
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:53,950
为什么
Why?

524
00:17:53,950 --> 00:17:55,780
菲尔 你不准再说了
Phil, don't you say another word!

525
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:56,440
看到没 告诉过你了
Ow! See? I told you.

526
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,790
这究竟是怎么一回事
What the hell is going on here?

527
00:17:57,790 --> 00:17:59,260
-什么事都没有 -菲尔
- Nothing. - Phil?

528
00:17:59,260 --> 00:17:59,990
好吧 如果你非得知道
Fine -- if you have to know

529
00:17:59,990 --> 00:18:02,480
我生活里的每一个细节的话
every last detail about my life...

530
00:18:02,530 --> 00:18:04,640
我在卡波和汤姆打赌输了 欠了他五顿饭
I lost a bet to Tom in Cabo. Now I owe him five meals.

531
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:06,300
-说完了 -就这回事
- There -- we're done. - That's it.

532
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:07,930
那你为什么不早说
Why didn't you just say that?

533
00:18:07,930 --> 00:18:10,420
没为什么
Th-- there's no reason.

534
00:18:10,870 --> 00:18:12,830
打的什么赌
What...was...the bet?

535
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:15,530
菲尔 我认真的 不准再说话了
Phil, I mean it -- don't say another word.

536
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,890
她们迟早会猜到的 汤姆
They're gonna figure it out, Tom.

537
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:19,270
-她们怎么可能猜到 -她们会猜到的
- How could they figure out, Phil? - They're gonna figure it out.

538
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:22,070
我们喝鸡尾酒喝醉了 然后我们想弄清
We were drunk on margaritas, and we wanted to find out

539
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:24,280
谁的老婆能吃更多的蟋蟀
whose wife would eat the most crickets.

540
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,150
-什么 -什么
- What?! - What?!

541
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,110
看来她们并没可能猜到 菲尔
Doesn't seem like they were circling that, Phil.

542
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:28,820
你们就抓了蟋蟀
You were just g-grabbing crickets

543
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,730
偷偷往我们的食物里放吗
and sneaking them into our food?

544
00:18:30,730 --> 00:18:32,840
不是活蟋蟀 烤的
Not live ones. They were roasted.

545
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,430
天啊
Oh, my god!

546
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:35,720
你们真恶心
You're disgusting people.

547
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,710
你没看到好的一面 亲爱的
You're missing the silver lining here, honey.

548
00:18:37,710 --> 00:18:39,250
我输掉了
I lost the bet.

549
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,390
所以我没吃成蟋蟀吗
So I didn't eat crickets?

550
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:41,580
你吃了三只
You ate three.

551
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:42,770
丽萨吃了六只
Ohh! Lisa had six.

552
00:18:42,770 --> 00:18:43,930
六只
Six?!

553
00:18:44,070 --> 00:18:45,140
你让我吃四只不就已经可以赢了吗
You could've won with four!

554
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:47,310
亲爱的 我不能冒这个险
Baby, baby, I couldn't take that chance.

555
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,800
我要让你们俩好好地思考一下
I'd like to give you two a little something to think about.

556
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,850
你们吃的大部分食物都是我们准备的
Most of the food you eat is prepared by us.

557
00:18:56,850 --> 00:18:58,210
或者是私人厨师准备的
Or by our private chef.

558
00:18:58,210 --> 00:18:59,570
但我懂你意思 你继续说
But I-I like where you're going.

559
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:02,020
下一回你们俩大嚼汉堡
Next time you take a bite of a big, juicy burger

560
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:03,600
或者吃意大利面时
or dig into a bowl of spaghetti,

561
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:06,060
里面会有一些特殊的佐料
there's gonna be an extra special ingredient in there,

562
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:08,110
绝对不是妻子的爱意
and it won't be love.

563
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,790
你这次放了几只
How many did you get this time?

564
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:16,840
两只蟋蟀
Two crickets.

565
00:19:20,990 --> 00:19:22,420
这才更有道理嘛
Okay, this makes more sense.

566
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:24,230
芭芭拉绝对不会让自家大门敞开的
Barbra would never leave her gate wide open.

567
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:25,310
我家的门是坏了关不上
They're broken, okay?

568
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:27,390
别让我后悔带你来这
Don't make me regret bringing you here.

569
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:29,820
谁
Hello?

570
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:31,430
芭芭拉在家吗 我是雷·利奥塔
Is Barbra home? It's Ray Liotta.

571
00:19:31,430 --> 00:19:32,530
演过《好家伙》
You know, from "Goodfellas."

572
00:19:32,530 --> 00:19:34,090
-《散弹露露》 -还有《梦幻成真》
- "Something Wild." - "Field of Dreams."

573
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:35,740
我知道他是谁 怎么了 雷
Oh, I know who he is. What's up, Ray?

574
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:37,260
芭芭拉 我这有些你的邮件
Barbra, I have some of your mail

575
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:39,170
寄到你原来在西达赫斯特的住处了
from when you used to live over at Cedarhurst.

576
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:40,860
我这还有个朋友想
And I have a friend here that would like --

577
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:43,630
把邮件放到门口 我叫人去拿
Just leave the mail by the gate. I'll send someone down.

578
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:44,650
好的 但是
O-okay, but --

579
00:19:44,650 --> 00:19:45,720
还有什么事
Oh. There's more?

580
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,770
史翠珊小姐 你好 我叫米奇尔·普里契特
Uh, Ms. Streisand, hi. My -- my name is Mitchell Pritchett,

581
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:51,050
不知道多少年前我就是你的粉丝了
And I have been a fan of yours since I can't even remember,

582
00:19:51,050 --> 00:19:52,730
您的风雅和正直
And -- oh, your artistry and integrity

583
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:54,900
影响了我的整个人生 我
has inspired me my whole life, and I just --

584
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:57,000
真不敢相信我在和你说话
I can't even believe I'm talking to you right now.

585
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:59,760
拜托 我只是个普通人 和你一样
Please. I'm just a regular person, like you.

586
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:02,570
我穿裤子都需要有人帮我一条腿一条腿往上套
I have people put on my pants one leg at a time.

587
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:03,860
太好笑了
That's so funny.

588
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:05,880
芭芭拉 今天是他的生日
Barbra, today is his birthday!

589
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:07,050
实际上应该是三周前
Well, technically, it was three weeks ago.

590
00:20:07,050 --> 00:20:08,090
-别搞砸了 -抱歉
- All right, you're blowing it. - Sorry.

591
00:20:08,090 --> 00:20:10,300
你的声音很甜美 米奇尔
You sound very sweet, Mitchell.

592
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:12,840
我在想 你也许可以送给他一个特殊的礼物
I-I was thinking maybe as a special treat, you could --

593
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,600
我才不要对着门禁话筒唱歌 雷
I'm not singing into my gate, Ray.

594
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,320
很荣幸跟您聊天
Well, it was very nice to talk to you.

595
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:17,620
我只有一个小小的问题
I did have a quick question about --

596
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:18,620
再见
Goodbye.

597
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:19,730
没事
It's fine.

598
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:21,790
等我讲这个故事的时候
When I tell the story,

599
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,740
结尾是她给我唱了生日歌
it ends with her singing "Happy Birthday."

600
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,710
糟糕 过三点了
Oh, shoot. It's past 3:00.

601
00:20:27,710 --> 00:20:29,260
怎么了 赶不上晚饭了吗
What's wrong? You late for dinner?

602
00:20:29,490 --> 00:20:29,990
杰
Jay.

603
00:20:29,990 --> 00:20:31,400
没事 如果我们现在走 我们
Honey, it's okay. If we leave now, we --

604
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,770
不 我错过了
No, no, I missed it.

605
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:33,890
你错过什么了
What did you miss?

606
00:20:33,890 --> 00:20:36,090
这周老电影频道上是舞蹈电影特映周
It's Fred and Ginger Week on TCM.

607
00:20:36,090 --> 00:20:38,530
今天播的《欢乐时光》[36年电影]我忘了录
They're showing "Swing Time". And I forgot to record it.

608
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:42,010
让我给你介绍一个新发明 叫网飞
Let me tell you about a little innovation called Netflix.

609
00:20:42,010 --> 00:20:43,530
你绝对不会再错过任何一部电影了
You'll never miss another movie again.

610
00:20:43,530 --> 00:20:45,180
-真的吗 -对天发誓
- Really? - Hand to God.

611
00:20:45,570 --> 00:20:47,320
你在电脑上挑一部电影
You pick a film on your computer.

612
00:20:47,810 --> 00:20:50,120
三天之后 电影光碟就邮到你家了
Three days later, there's a disk in your mailbox.

613
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:52,410
你可得跟上科技的脚步啊 马蒂
You got to stay up with technology, Marty.

614
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,960
谢谢
Wow. Thanks.

615
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,940
你能相信他居然不知道网上直播吗
Can you believe he doesn't know about streaming?

616
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,540
如果没那玩意儿 我还不如死了好
If I ever get that out of touch, kill me.
